# --- Deployment checkpoints (issue #176) ---
# Per-contract IDs and transaction results are persisted as recoverable run
# artifacts after each successful deploy/init operation. The workflow writes
# one checkpoint file per operation under deployed/checkpoints/ and appends a
# line here so a partially completed run can be resumed without redeploying
# contracts that already succeeded.
#
# Checkpoint format (one line per completed operation):
#   checkpoint.<contract>.<op>=<status>;tx=<tx_hash>;id=<contract_id>;at=<iso8601>
#
# Resume procedure:
#   1. Download the latest `deploy-checkpoints-<network>` run artifact (or read
#      the checkpoint lines below) from the interrupted workflow run.
#   2. Re-run the workflow with `resume=true` (workflow_dispatch input). The
#      workflow skips any contract whose checkpoint status is `success` and
#      continues from the first missing/failed operation.
#   3. Verify the final manifest matches the checkpointed IDs before promoting.
#
# Example checkpoint lines (populated by the workflow at runtime):
# checkpoint.vault_registry.deploy=success;tx=0xabc...;id=CAVRZ...;at=2026-07-06T11:16:43Z
# checkpoint.vault_registry.init=success;tx=0xdef...;id=CAVRZ...;at=2026-07-06T11:16:50Z
#
# --- Post-init readback checks (issue #177) ---
# After each successful init invocation the workflow reads back the on-chain
# admin and stored version for the contract and compares them to the intended
# values. A mismatch fails the run before the deployment is recorded as
# completed (no `checkpoint.<contract>.init=success` line is written).
#
# Readback format (one line per verified contract):
#   readback.<contract>=ok;admin=<address>;version=<version>;at=<iso8601>
#
# Example readback lines (populated by the workflow at runtime):
# readback.vault_registry=ok;admin=GADMIN...;version=1.0.0;at=2026-07-06T11:16:52Z
#
# --- Manifest validation (issue #178) ---
# Before this file is committed, the deploy workflow validates the manifest:
# every required contract ID, its version, the network, and the deployed_at
# timestamp must be present and well-formed. Missing or malformed values fail
# the run with a clear error and nothing is committed.
#
# Required keys (all must be present and non-empty):
#   vault_registry, vault_registry_version
#   access_lease, access_lease_version
#   subscription, subscription_version
#   network, deployed_at
#
# Format rules:
#   <contract>          Stellar contract ID: 56 chars, starts with 'C', base32 [A-Z2-7]
#   <contract>_version  Semver: MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH (e.g. 1.0.0)
#   network             One of: testnet, mainnet, futurenet
#   deployed_at         ISO-8601 UTC timestamp (e.g. 2026-07-06T11:16:43Z)
